NOTES=["Training loop (inner): Lagoon -> Staghorn Forest (S1) -> Bommie crest -> Mangrove drift -> Lagoon. About 2 min; sharks can't follow through S1's anemone row without breaking coral (loud).",
"Training loop (outer): Bommie -> Surge Channel (4 s ride) -> Wall -> Sand edge -> Flats -> Maze mouth -> Maze (B4) -> Forest gate -> Bommie. 5 min; crosses every apex lane once.",
"Blood flow: the tide runs Lagoon -> Forest -> Flats -> Wall on the ebb and reverses on the flood every 4 minutes (the tide mill shows which). Blood on the Flats reaches the Wall and its sharks in 40 s on the ebb.",
"Sightlines: corridors 8-12 m; Bommie top 25 m; Flats 60 m+; Wall 40 m vertical. Alarm regions: Reef (Lagoon, Nursery, Forest, Bommie, Maze) and Open (Flats, Beach, Hole, Wall); the Raiders enter at the Wall by turtle and inland by B4.",
"Coral erosion: each crown-of-thorns eats one staghorn segment per 90 s; a broken segment turns a corridor into a lane sharks can use. Shark rams also break segments (2 noise).",
"The dolphin pod follows the divers' centroid at 20-30 m while allied; rams any shark that enters 10 m of a diver; turns hostile for the match the moment a dolphin takes damage from a diver."]
BOSS=["The Matriarch — an orca matriarch (size 6) with a pod of three (size 5, 3,000 HP each). Arena: the Drop-off Wall and the Blue Hole until tide 12; after that the Flats and the Lagoon too (the whole map except the corridors, which are too narrow).",
"HP 15,000 (x1.08 per tide); weak points: the blowhole (when she surfaces to breathe every 90 s, 4 s window) and the belly (when the surge channel trap flips her, 4 s). Skin halves damage elsewhere.",
"Phase 1 (100-60%): the pod hunts as one. Herd (the pod fans wide and pushes divers off cover), then Ram from her. She stays in open water; divers under table coral are safe from her but not from the pod.",
"Phase 2 (60-30%): once two pod members are dead she charges in straight lines (predictable, dodgeable, 8 m knockback) and uses Tail Slap on coral to collapse cover; she calls the third pod member back from wherever it is.",
"Phase 3 (30-0%): she rams the Bommie itself (the cleaning station collapses; every host on the map gains +20% aggression), breaches into the Lagoon shallows where she's slow, and Bites to carry divers into the blue.",
"Arena rules: the surge channel trap flips her for 4 s if she's in the channel (lure her with a Chummer); the Shaman's drum (taken from a Raider) calls her AND raises her aggression, so it's a weapon and a mistake; dolphins allied to the divers harass her (-10% her speed) until she kills them.",
"Kill reward: 1,500 base scrip x tide, a Locker weapon each, and the Shaman's drum if not already held. The pod flees when she dies. She returns to the Wall after 6 minutes at 50% HP with a new pod."]
FACTION=dict(name="The Reef Raiders",intro="The Island tribe on a hunting raid: free-divers who breathe at the surface and ride sea turtles between the reef and the blue. They hunt beasts for meat and leave corpses everywhere they go, so a raid raises blood wherever it passes; their Shaman's drum turns the reef itself against the divers.",
units=[("Spear Diver",130,"Coral spear","35 melee, 0.9 s; thrown 45 (one throw, then retrieves)","Fast in water (2.2); must surface every 60 s (they use mangrove roots and the Bommie top)","Hunts in pairs; flanks through corridors","Exhales a bubble stream before a lunge; surfaces predictably","220 scrip"),
("Turtle Rider",160,"Lance from turtle-back","50 charge","Turtle speed (1.6) but never surfaces (the turtle breathes)","Charges down the Flats and the Wall; the turtle is a shield (armored front)","The turtle's flippers churn sand","Turtle (becomes a neutral Green Turtle if the rider dies), 260"),
("Sling Diver",110,"Sling: coconut bombs","40 blast, 2 m radius","Diver speed","Lobs from 15 m; targets divers in the open","Whirls the sling twice","Coconut bombs (3 tactical), 240"),
("Netter",150,"Reed net","Holds 4 s","Diver speed","Nets a diver at a corridor mouth for the spears","Spreads the net wide","Net Gun, 250"),
("Shaman (Hunts)",800,"The drum","0","Slow; rides a turtle","Drums from the Wall: +aggression to every beast in 40 m for 20 s; calls sharks on the third drum and the Matriarch on the fifth","Raises the drum overhead; each beat is a 6-noise pulse","The drum (a usable item: 5 uses), 600")],
tactics=["Squads arrive at the Wall on turtles and ride the Flats toward the Maze mouth, or come inland by B4 (Raider Road) on foot; they know the Reacher gates and jump them.",
"On contact: the Netter nets the lead diver, Spear Divers flank through the nearest corridor, the Sling Diver lobs from open water, the Turtle Rider charges anyone on the Flats.",
"They hunt beasts on the way in for meat (they'll spear a dugong or a turtle if they pass one), which drops corpses and calls sharks onto everyone; they shoot dolphins on purpose to turn the pod on the divers.",
"They avoid the Blue Hole and the deep Wall (they must surface). Trapping them in the Flats far from the surface makes them retreat to the Bommie top, where the cleaning station calms the sharks they've called.",
"In a Hunt the Shaman drums from the Wall on his turtle; every fifth beat can call the Matriarch. Kill him first, or take the drum and beat it near the Raiders."],
barks=["Spotting: 'Brass-heads on our reef.' / 'Take their meat.'","Spearing a beast: 'Good eating.' / 'Let the blood bring the big ones.'","Dolphin shot: 'Now the grey ones hate them too!'","Netting: 'Wrapped. Bring the spears.'","Retreat: 'To the coral head. The little fish will calm the sharks.'","Shaman: 'The sea's mother hears the drum.' / 'Five beats and she comes.'"])
